    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (12 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner read model.\n\n**How the response is built:** `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns an `OwnerDto`, which is generated from the OpenAPI spec (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) and populated by the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the same place the existing `displayName` derived field is computed.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets an `initials` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `initials` computing the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n       + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nFor `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec and the new `Cp06Tests`. `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty` on `Person` and required by the create endpoint, so both are always present and non-empty by the time an owner is mapped back.",
